    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_00cc5fca838e5b1f268dfae2ac2c592a87f96281b93fc8dc16f0e2ee9a6e57fa",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The two logarithms become comparable only after different reductions expose linear Gaussian coordinates: the matrix logarithm is expanded in trace powers, while log zeta is replaced in normalized L2 by a short prime Dirichlet sum. The resulting array arguments share variance convergence and removal of a high-mode or large-prime tail, but the arithmetic side additionally has to replace independent circle phases by finite-time prime phases through quantitative equidistribution.",
